From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] UsbNetwork: assume media on a point-to-point gadget

edk2's USB-net stack starts CableDetect = 0 and only raises it on catching a
CDC NETWORK_CONNECTION / NETWORK_CONNECTED notification. Linux's gadget
functions (f_ecm and f_ncm alike) emit those only on link-state changes, and
the enumeration-time one fires long before the UEFI driver binds, so it is
effectively never set: the first request over the link fails with
EFI_NO_MEDIA.

That model suits a dongle with an RJ45, where the cable really can be absent.
It does not suit a point-to-point gadget, where enumeration *is* the proof of
link -- there is no second connector to unplug. On this board the only USB
NIC is the BMC's CDC-NCM host interface (see RpiRedfishPkg), which is exactly
that.

Default the initialiser to 1, and make the flag sticky thereafter: a host
warm reset makes the gadget queue a NETWORK_DISCONNECT that the freshly bound
driver would read as "cable unplugged" for the rest of the boot, the matching
CONNECTED having been emitted while nothing was listening.

Same change as nuc-bios-build's 0019 patch (CDC-ECM/JetKVM), regenerated
against the NumberOneGit fork.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform specific]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbNetwork/NetworkCommon/DriverBinding.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbNetwork/NetworkCommon/DriverBinding.c
@@ -288,7 +288,7 @@
 
   NicDevice->NicInfo.UsbEth         = UsbEth;
   NicDevice->NicInfo.MaxSegmentSize = (UINT16)BulkDataSize;
-  NicDevice->NicInfo.CableDetect    = 0;
+  NicDevice->NicInfo.CableDetect    = 1;  // RpiRedfish: point-to-point NCM gadget, enumeration is the link proof
   NicDevice->ReceiveBuffer          = ALIGN_POINTER ((VOID *)NicDevice, 4096);
 
   CopyMem ((CHAR8 *)&(NicDevice->NicInfo.MacAddr), (CHAR8 *)&MacAddress, sizeof (MacAddress));
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbNetwork/NetworkCommon/PxeFunction.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbNetwork/NetworkCommon/PxeFunction.c
@@ -455,7 +455,7 @@
 
   if (Cdb->OpFlags == PXE_OPFLAGS_INITIALIZE_DETECT_CABLE) {
     if ((Nic->Request.Request == USB_CDC_NETWORK_CONNECTION) && (Nic->Request.Value == NETWORK_DISCONNECT)) {
-      Nic->CableDetect = 0;
+      Nic->CableDetect = 1;  // RpiRedfish: link is point-to-point
     } else if ((Nic->Request.Request == USB_CDC_NETWORK_CONNECTION) && (Nic->Request.Value == NETWORK_CONNECTED)) {
       Nic->CableDetect = 1;
     }
@@ -1195,7 +1195,7 @@
   }
 
   if ((Nic->Request.Request == USB_CDC_NETWORK_CONNECTION) && (Nic->Request.Value == NETWORK_DISCONNECT)) {
-    Nic->CableDetect = 0;
+    Nic->CableDetect = 1;  // RpiRedfish: link is point-to-point
   } else if ((Nic->Request.Request == USB_CDC_NETWORK_CONNECTION) && (Nic->Request.Value == NETWORK_CONNECTED)) {
     Nic->CableDetect = 1;
   }
